# Monitor-wifi docs are staging notes for in-flux named-radio work and stay
# untracked by default: bring-up logs, captures (*.pcap), firmware blobs, and
# port references that churn faster than review can follow.
#
# The exceptions below are the named-radio DOCTRINE — the rules the in-tree
# design docs are reviewed against (no host addressing, the name is the
# addressing, peers are data too). Until 2026-07-16 the doctrine was ignored
# while the plan that violates it (ndn-face-wifi-aware/docs/) was tracked and
# reviewed. A doctrine that is not in the repo cannot guard the repo, so the
# doctrine files are versioned. `*` still covers everything else in this
# directory, including anything binary that lands here later.
#
# RADIO_SUBSYSTEM.md is versioned for the same reason: its §2 ("IP radio vs named
# radio") is the clearest statement of the thesis anywhere in the workspace, and
# its §4.1 is where the NAN stack is reconciled with it. Doctrine that reviewers
# cannot see is doctrine that cannot object.
*
!.gitignore
!named-radio.md
!named-radio-vision-frontier.md
!RADIO_SUBSYSTEM.md
!mac-addressing-doctrine.md
!named-token-scheduling.md
!cclf-named-mac.md
!time-slice-mac.md
!timing-rides-named-data.md
!named-filter-mac-redesign.md
!mac-design-roots.md
!named-radio-primer.md
